From: NixOS DTrace maintainers
Subject: dtrace: authorize tracing using the effective user ID

The NixOS module grants selected members of the dtrace group access through a
group-restricted, setuid-root wrapper.  Such a process retains the caller's
real user ID while acquiring an effective user ID of zero.  Checking the real
ID therefore rejects tracing even though the operating system has already
authorized and elevated the invocation.

Use the effective ID for this frontend privilege check.  This makes the check
honor the wrapper's security boundary; access to that wrapper remains limited
to explicitly configured, fully trusted users.

diff --git a/cmd/dtrace.c b/cmd/dtrace.c
index a2d44f61..ba0f63ef 100644
--- a/cmd/dtrace.c
+++ b/cmd/dtrace.c
@@ -1044,7 +1044,7 @@ main(int argc, char **argv)
 	 * DMODE_EXEC with g_exec==0, since otherwise too many probes will
 	 * simply not be recognized, likely causing puzzling behavior.
 	 */
-	if (getuid() != 0 && (g_mode == DMODE_LIST || g_mode == DMODE_EXEC)) {
+	if (geteuid() != 0 && (g_mode == DMODE_LIST || g_mode == DMODE_EXEC)) {
 		fprintf(stderr, "%s: run as root for tracing and listing probes\n", g_pname);
 		return E_USAGE;
 	}
